BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Returning to Ourselves | Curatorial Tour with Lisa Deanne Smith
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261202T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261202T183000
UID:returning-ourselves-curatorial-tour-lisa-deanne-smith@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Returning to Ourselves: Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird—
 A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings Curatorial Tour 
 with Lisa Deanne Smith\n\nReturning to Ourselves: Rebecca Baird and Kenny 
 Alvin Baird—A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings Cu
 ratorial Tour with Lisa Deanne Smith\, Wednesday\, December 02\, 2026\, 5:
 00 p.m. to 6:30 p.m.\, Onsite Gallery\, 199 Richmond Street West\, Toronto
  Join exhibition curator Lisa Deanne Smith for an engaging and in-depth cu
 ratorial tour of Returning to Ourselves: Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Bai
 rd—A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings . During th
 is guided experience\, Lisa will share behind-the-scenes insights into the
  exhibition’s development\, exploring the artistic practices\, personal 
 histories\, and creative journeys of siblings Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvi
 n Baird. This intimate tour offers a unique opportunity to learn more abou
 t the curatorial process\, the relationships that shaped the exhibition\, 
 and the powerful themes woven throughout the artists’ decades-long bodie
 s of work. About the Curator Lisa Deanne Smith is Senior Curator of Onsite
  Gallery at OCAD University. Her curatorial practice examines voice\, embo
 died knowledge\, non-human–centred worldviews\, and the processes throug
 h which knowledge is created and shared. As part of this inquiry\, Smith b
 ecame a certified Forest Therapy guide\, deepening her engagement with lan
 d-based learning. Recent curatorial projects include The Sunshine Eaters \
 , How to Breathe Forever \, power \, and How will we be with you? These mu
 ltidisciplinary exhibitions included works by Mary Anne Barkhouse\, Bonave
 nture Soh Bejeng Ndikung\, Shary Boyle\, Nick Cave\, Rocky Dobey\, John Gr
 eyson\, Brian Jungen\, Jessica Karuhanga\, Natalie King\, Qavavau Manumie\
 , Ekow Nimako\, Alanis Obomsawin\, Ebony G. Patterson\, Rajni Perera\, Pej
 vak\, and Winnie Truong\, among others. About the Exhibition Returning to 
 Ourselves: Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird—A Retrospective of Art an
 d Design by Cree Métis Siblings presents over forty years of transformati
 ve work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculp
 ture\, painting\, and traditional material practices\, alongside interior 
 design\, film art direction\, graphic design\, and public art commissions.
  Emerging from their Cree Métis histories and ways of knowing\, the Baird
 s approach creative practice through multiple cultural perspectives\, brin
 ging together diverse forms of making grounded in lived experience\, colla
 boration\, and community-centred practice. Visit Registration Page
LOCATION:Onsite Gallery (RHD) 199 Richmond Street West 199 Richmond Street
  West
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/returning-ourselves-curato
 rial-tour-lisa-deanne-smith
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:OCAD University Senate Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T151500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T173000
UID:ocad-university-senate-meeting-21@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:OCAD University Senate Meeting\n\nThe next regular meeting of 
 the OCAD University Senate is scheduled to take place on Monday\, November
  30\, 2026 from 3:15 pm – 5:30 pm EDT. The Senate is responsible for the
  establishment and regulation of academic policy\, standards and procedure
 s at OCAD University. The Senate and its many committees are in charge of 
 all matters pertaining to OCAD U academic resources\, academic programming
 \, academic strategic planning\, student affairs and any other such matter
 s relating to academic issues. More information can be found on the OCAD U
  Senate webpage . If you would like to attend as a guest\, or if you have 
 any questions\, please contact David Wagschal\, Quality Assurance Officer 
 & Associate Senate Secretary at dwagschal@ocadu.ca . Please note: Requests
  to attend public meetings must be made at least one business day in advan
 ce of the meeting .
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/ocad-university-senate-mee
 ting-21
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
