BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EXPERIENCE CREATE: Notebook Binding Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T170000
UID:experience-create-notebook-binding-workshop@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Notebook Binding with Printmaking & Publications\, part of Alu
 mni Relations' November workshop series.\n\nNotebook Binding with Printmak
 ing & Publications Dates: Saturday\, November 28th Location: Room 387 3rd 
 Floor\, 100 McCaul St. Time: 12:15pm to 1:00pm: Welcome Reception 1:00pm t
 o 5:00pm: Workshop Cost: $30 per person All materials provided Hosted by P
 rintmaking & Publications alum Laur Flom\, this one-day introductory works
 hop will teach participants how to bind their own hard-cover notebook from
  start to finish. Participants will take home one handmade notebook. This 
 workshop is great for artists\, writers\, and designers of all backgrounds
 . No prior experience necessary. Laur Flom is a printmaker and OCAD Univer
 sity Printmaking alum (2022). They hold an MFA from Emily Carr University 
 of Art and Design. Utilizing the sequential nature of print and book forms
 \, their work explores themes of queerness and absurdism. Laur's recent wo
 rk centers around pushing the limits of what books can be. Their work is h
 eld in various public and private collections\, including the Thomas Fishe
 r Rare Book Library\, and Emily Carr University's Special Collections libr
 ary.
LOCATION:Main Building & Rosalie Sharp Centre for Design (MCA) 100 McCaul 
 Street Room 387
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/experience-create-notebook
 -binding-workshop
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EXPERIENCE CREATE: Sculpting from Life
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T160000
UID:experience-create-sculpting-life@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Sculpting from Life with Associate Professor Francis LeBouthil
 ler\, part of Alumni Relations' November workshop series.\n\nSculpting fro
 m Life with Associate Professor Francis LeBouthiller Dates: Saturday\, Nov
 ember 28th Location: Room 617 6th Floor\, 100 McCaul St. Time: 12:15pm to 
 1:00pm: Welcome Reception 1:00pm to 4:00pm: Workshop Cost: $30 per person 
 All materials provided In this hands-on workshop\, participants will use r
 aw clay to sculpt from a live model under the guidance of Associate Profes
 sor\, Francis Lebouthillier. Participants should wear comfortable clothes 
 and shoes they don’t mind getting dirty. Francis LeBouthillier is a Toro
 nto-based multi-disciplinary artist\, designer\, researcher and educator. 
 Since 1989\, Francis has been an Associate Professor at OCAD University\, 
 where he teaches in the Faculty of Art. For over 20 years\, Francis has ma
 intained a research practice that involves developing high-fidelity surgic
 al simulators and medical models . This work has involved research teams a
 t Toronto's Mount Sinai Hospital\, Women's College Hospital\, and the Univ
 ersity of Toronto's Surgical Skills Lab.
LOCATION:Main Building & Rosalie Sharp Centre for Design (MCA) 100 McCaul 
 Street Room 617
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/experience-create-sculptin
 g-life
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
