SUMMARY:Design a Sharps Container!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T160000
UID:design-sharps-container@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:SWC x Student Union\n\nThe Student Wellness Centre within OCAD
  U has partnered with the Student Union\, for our first bi-weekly Harm Red
 uction Drop In. Come join us\, and design your own sharps container! We wi
 ll have food\, crafts\, and harm reduction supplies available. This worksh
 op will allow for students to learn and ask questions about Harm Reduction
  (ie: safer drug use practices\, the toxic Toronto drug supply\, naloxone 
 training\, drug prohibition/mass incarceration\, HIV and Hep C) and to pro
 vide input on how the SWC can improve the program. We will also have conve
 rsations around the implementation and design of permanent sharps containe
 rs on our campus. To sign up\, email Chance at ccordon@ocadu.ca More to co
 me!
LOCATION:230 Richmond (RHB) 230 Richmond St. W Student Living Room\, 8th f
 loor.
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/design-sharps-container
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Should I Go to Graduate School: Deciding When\, Why & Where
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T140000
UID:should-i-go-graduate-school-deciding-when-why-where@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Graduate school can be an exciting next step\, but it isn't th
 e only path forward. In this interactive workshop\, you'll consider whethe
 r further study aligns with your creative practice and career goals\, then
  learn how to identify graduate programs that match your priorities. You'l
 l leave with a personalized set of criteria to help guide your research an
 d future decisions.\n\nShould I Go to Graduate School: Deciding When\, Why
  & Where Date/Time: Wednesday\, November 18\, 2026\, 1:00 - 2:00 p.m. Loca
 tion: CEAD\, 115 McCaul St. Level 3 RSVP to attend Graduate school can be 
 an exciting next step\, but it isn't the only path forward. In this intera
 ctive workshop\, you'll consider whether further study aligns with your cr
 eative practice and career goals\, then learn how to identify graduate pro
 grams that match your priorities. You'll leave with a personalized set of 
 criteria to help guide your research and future decisions. Learning Outcom
 es: Clarify why you are considering graduate school. Consider whether grad
 uate school makes sense now\, later\, or perhaps not at all. Identify pers
 onal priorities for selecting a graduate programme. Compare programmes usi
 ng fit\, structure\, resources\, costs\, location and outcomes.
LOCATION:Rosalie Sharp Pavillion (MCD) 115 McCaul St. Level 3
URL:https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/7M0TcEmxsw
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
