BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Workshop Series: A Painting as a Composite Material
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T170000
UID:workshop-series-painting-composite-material@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Saturday workshop series with Professor Lauchlan Reid\, Co-Dir
 ector of the Sustainable Colour Lab.\n\nA Painting as a Composite Material
  Presented in a down-to-earth and approachable format\, this 3-week\, in-d
 epth workshop series with Professor Lauchlan Reid will provide a comprehen
 sive and interactive discussion of the physical properties that determine 
 the quality and longevity of a painting. With detailed examples and qualit
 ative breakdowns of the factors at play with painting supports\, grounds\,
  paints\, mediums\, varnishes\, and frames\, this series dispels the myths
  under which many artists operate and provides them the basis to make info
 rmed decisions and choices\, while providing their artworks a sense of qua
 lity and longevity that is otherwise relegated to museums and conservators
 . Dates: Saturday\, November 14th\, 21st & 28th Location: Room 466 4th Flo
 or\, 100 McCaul St. Time: 12:15pm to 1:00pm: Welcome Reception* 1:00pm to 
 5:00pm: Workshop *Welcome reception will be hosted on November 14th only. 
 Cost: $100 per person All materials provided Lauchlan Reid is an artist\, 
 illustrator and educator based in Hamilton and Toronto\, Ontario. Founder 
 of noted illustration and art collective Team Macho\, Reid's art and desig
 n practice spans all media and methodologies\, including drawing\, paintin
 g\, sculpture\, installation\, publishing\, animation\, and printmaking. L
 auchlan is a tenured Associate Professor and former Program Chair of the I
 llustration Program at OCAD University and is a co-director of the OCAD U 
 Sustainable Colour Lab \, a research initiative aimed at the resurrection 
 of "lost" techniques and materials from natural\, historical sources. *Ple
 ase note: due to limited seats\, this series is only open to OCAD U Alumni
 .
LOCATION:Main Building & Rosalie Sharp Centre for Design (MCA) 100 McCaul 
 Street Room MCA 466
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/workshop-series-painting-c
 omposite-material
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
