BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rooted & Restless
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T193000
UID:rooted-restless@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Rooted & Restless (featuring Dr. Amanda White\, Dr. Ian Clarke
 \, and Dr. Vanessa Harden)\n\nGenerously supported by BMO. The Global Cent
 re for Climate Action welcomes Dr. Amanda White\, Canada Research Chair in
  Sustainability\, Ecological Justice\, and Climate Action in Creative Prac
 tices from Emily Carr University of Art and Design (ECUAD) alongside Dr. I
 an Clarke\, Associate Professor from the Faculty of Arts and Sciences at O
 CAD University\, and Dr. Vanessa Harden\, Director of BioLink Designs to e
 xplore the future of transdisciplinary research\, the possibilities of ind
 eterminate growth\, and new approaches to ecological engagement. The prese
 ntations will be followed by a seed ball making workshop. No experience re
 quired to attend the workshop – just a willingness to get your hands dir
 ty! Workshop Registration Link: https://luma.com/mjqlzulc Introducing: Dr.
  Amanda White\, Canada Research Chair in Sustainability\, Ecological Justi
 ce\, and Climate Action in Creative Practices\, Emily Carr University Aman
 da White (she/her) is Canada Research Chair in Sustainability\, Ecological
  Justice\, and Climate action in Creative Practices at Emily Carr Universi
 ty\, on unceded Musqueam\, Squamish and Tsleil-Waututh territories. She is
  an artist\, researcher\, and currently leads the Living Environmental Art
 s and Futures (LEAF) Kitchen & Lab at ECU\, a new space supporting environ
 mentally engaged creative research and practices including a focus on plan
 ts studies\, food justice and living systems. She co-edited the book Ecolo
 gies in Practice: Environmentally Engaged Arts in Canada (Wilfrid Laurier 
 University Press\, 2024) and recently published a graphic novel for middle
  grade readers about food security. With: Dr. Ian Clarke\, Co-Director\, B
 ADLab\, and Associate Professor\, OCAD University Ian Clarke is an Associa
 te Professor of sustainability and biology at OCAD University. He holds a 
 Ph.D. (Biochemistry) from Queen’s University and an AOCAD (printmaking).
  He trained as a Biologist at the Design Table (BaDT) at the Biomimicry In
 stitute. Prior to moving to OCAD\, he was a cancer stem-cell researcher at
  the Hospital for Sick Children (Toronto). He has co-authored numerous sci
 entific articles in journals such as Nature\, and the Proceedings of the N
 ational Academy of Science (USA). His publications have received over 23\,
 000 citations in peer reviewed journals. His current research focuses clim
 ate change adaptation through sustainable biomaterials\, as well as urban 
 agriculture and food systems. Dr. Vanessa Harden\, Director\, BioLink Desi
 gns Vanessa Harden is an artist\, designer\, and researcher working at the
  intersection of urban ecology\, climate resilience\, and public space. Sh
 e holds a Doctor of Design from Harvard University’s Graduate School of 
 Design\, where her research explored how mycorrhizal fungal networks can r
 econnect fragmented urban forests. She is the founder of Wild Flag Studios
 \, Subversive Gardener\, and BioLink Designs\, initiatives that bridge pub
 lic art\, ecological research\, and regenerative urban design. Her work ha
 s been exhibited internationally\, including at the Venice Biennale and Lo
 ndon’s V&A Museum. Through research\, design\, and community engagement\
 , she explores how cities can become more ecologically connected\, resilie
 nt\, and biodiverse.
LOCATION:Main Building & Rosalie Sharp Centre for Design (MCA) 100 McCaul 
 Street MCA 190 for the presentations and MCA 460 for the workshop
URL:https://luma.com/mjqlzulc
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:OCAD U X Reel Asian 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261121T235959
UID:ocad-u-x-reel-asian-2026@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:The 2026 edition of Reel Asian celebrates the 30th anniversary
  of the festival. In-person programming runs from Nov 11. to 21 with event
 s across Toronto\, including at OCAD University. Online events will take p
 lace from Nov. 16 to 29.\n\nThe Toronto Reel Asian International Film Fest
 ival ® is a unique showcase of contemporary cinema and works by Asia\, As
 ian diaspora\, and Asian Canadian filmmakers and creatives. Works include 
 films and videos by Asian-identifying artists in Canada\, the U.S.\, Asia 
 and all over the world. As Canada’s largest pan-Asian film festival\, Re
 el Asian ® provides a public forum for Asian media artists and their work
 \, and fuels the growing appreciation for Asian cinema in Canada. The 2026
  edition of Reel Asian celebrates the 30th anniversary of the festival. In
 -person programming runs from Nov 11. to 21 with events across Toronto\, i
 ncluding at OCAD University. Online events will take place from Nov. 16 to
  29. This year\, OCAD U is pleased to host a variety of exhibitions and vi
 rtual reality projects as part of the festival. Visit reelasian.com/festiv
 al for more info. Tickets on sale now! Use the code REELASIAN30 for 15% of
 f tickets.\n\nPalace Immersive Goong (이머시브궁) (Nov. 12 to 21)\n\n
 Join a multi-user VR journey set in Korea's iconic Gyeongbokgung Palace\, 
 where the grandeur of the Joseon Dynasty’s last unrealized royal banquet
  comes to life. More than a spectator\, you are a part of the celebration 
 in this cutting-edge\, location-based entertainment experience that seamle
 ssly blends history\, culture\, and technology in real time. Location : Op
 en Space Gallery\, 49 McCaul St.\, OCAD University Dates : Nov. 12 to 21\,
  12 to 5 p.m. Tickets : Pay what you can\n\nMeans to Enfold (Nov. 13 to 19
 )\n\nMeans to Enfold is an embrace\, a remembrance\, and a suggestion towa
 rds the ways we hold each other together through collective expression. In
  bringing together interactive installations\, a travelling exhibit of wor
 ks developed at the SSX x InterAccess AR residency\, a curated section of 
 student works created in Tech Jams and invited artworks by artists part of
  the inaugural SSX Artist Residency\, this community showcase highlights h
 ow collaboration can be a potent means to enfold the meanings in all our r
 elations. Drop by for the Means to Enfold opening reception on Friday\, No
 v. 13 from 7:30 to 11 p.m.\, featuring live music and refreshments. Bring 
 your infectious energies to the SSX Sing-Along Karaoketo to end the evenin
 g at a high note. All singing styles and music genres welcome! Location : 
 Open Space Gallery\, 49 McCaul St.\, OCAD University Dates : Nov. 13 to No
 v 19\, 12 to 5 p.m. Tickets : Free\n\nExpanded Dis/Closures Fireside Chat:
  Ana Serrano & Romeo Candido (Nov. 13)\n\nOCAD U President and Vice-Chance
 llor Ana Serrano (left) and director\, writer and composer Romeo Candido (
 right). Join this fireside chat with Ana Serrano\, president and vice-chan
 cellor of OCAD University and recipient of Reel Asian's 2026 Fire Horse Aw
 ard\, and Romeo Candido\, Emmy-nominated director\, writer\, composer\, an
 d Canadian Screen Award-winning producer working across film\, television\
 , theatre\, and music. They will open the Expanded Dis/Closures exhibition
  and conference with this fireside chat discussing ever-changing media and
  the role of creators in the challenges of our time. The fireside chat wil
 l be followed by the Sari-Sari Reception at 7 p.m. Location : OCAD Univers
 ity Auditorium\, 100McCaul St.\, OCAD University Dates : Nov. 13\, 7 p.m. 
 Tickets : Free\n\nExpanded Dis/Closures - XR Summit (Nov. 16)\n\nReel Asia
 n’s XR Summit is a space for dialogue between emerging and established a
 rtists and studios\, professionals from the industry\, media scholars and 
 the wider communities who will connect and explore the state of the creati
 ve industries and the market trends leading innovation within the domains 
 of XR and spatial media\, both globally and locally. Location : School of 
 Graduate Studies\, 205 Richmond St. W.\, OCAD University Dates : Nov. 16\,
  10 a.m. to 7 p.m. Tickets : Free
LOCATION:Off Campus Marina Quay West\, 539 Queens Quay West
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/ocad-u-x-reel-asian-2026
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
